LLULLIAN COMBINATORY OPERATOR SYSTEM
====================================
→ 160 Logic

Formal structure of the Art (ternary phase), with types, variables,
counting, group action, composition, correlatives, and SID-PED map.

0. FUNDAMENTALS
---------------
The Art is a typed, multi-sorted, rotationally equivariant combinatory
system. Generators are a finite alphabet of polymorphic labels. Each
label simultaneously names an absolute principle, a relative principle,
a question-rule, a subject on the ladder of being, a virtue, and a vice.
Wheels implement a cyclic group action that enumerates compositions.

Historical cardinality:
  Standard ternary Art uses n = 9 letters:
    Lambda = { B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, K }
  Letter A is reserved for the centre of Figure A (God / coincidence
  of all dignities). A is not rotated on the volvelles.
  Earlier quaternary versions used 16 dignities.
  If a 10-letter set A = { A, B, ..., K } is used, treat A as a fixed
  point and restrict the cyclic action to the remaining 9 letters.

Six parallel sorts (columns) for every letter:

  Letter | Dignity (Fig.A)      | Relative (Fig.T)   | Question/Rule
  -------|----------------------|--------------------|----------------------
  B      | Bonitas              | Differentia        | Utrum?
  C      | Magnitudo            | Concordantia       | Quid?
  D      | Aeternitas / Duratio | Contrarietas       | De quo?
  E      | Potestas             | Principium         | Quare?
  F      | Sapientia            | Medium             | Quantum?
  G      | Voluntas             | Finis              | Quale?
  H      | Virtus               | Maioritas          | Quando?
  I      | Veritas              | Aequalitas         | Ubi?
  K      | Gloria               | Minoritas          | Quomodo / cum quo?

  Letter | Subject          | Virtue       | Vice
  -------|------------------|--------------|----------------
  B      | Deus             | Iustitia     | Avaritia
  C      | Angelus          | Prudentia    | Gula
  D      | Caelum           | Fortitudo    | Luxuria
  E      | Homo             | Temperantia  | Superbia
  F      | Imaginativa      | Fides        | Acedia
  G      | Sensitiva        | Spes         | Invidia
  H      | Vegetativa       | Caritas      | Ira
  I      | Elementativa     | Patientia    | Mendacium
  K      | Instrumentativa  | Pietas       | Inconstantia

Correlatives (internal triad of each dignity):
  For Bonitas:  agent = bonificativum
                patient = bonificabile
                act = bonificare
  Same pattern for every other dignity. These supply dynamics that
  a static pairing of letters would otherwise lack.

Letters are labelled constants, not free variables. Their "variability"
is only which sort (column) is active in a given reading.

1. TYPES AND INTERPRETATIONS
----------------------------
Sort set:
  S = { Dig, Rel, Q, Subj, Virt, Vic }

Each letter lambda in Lambda is a polymorphic constant:
  [[lambda]] : S -> Terms

Examples:
  [[B]](Dig)  = Bonitas
  [[B]](Rel)  = Differentia
  [[B]](Q)    = Utrum?
  [[B]](Subj) = Deus
  ...

Typed atom: pair (lambda, s) with lambda in Lambda, s in S.

Well-formed propositions typically take first atom as subject
(Dignity or Subject) and second as predicate (Dignity, Relative,
Virtue, ...).

2. COMBINATORIAL SPACES AND COUNTING
------------------------------------
Variables:
  n = |Lambda|          (historically 9; source note used 10)
  r = arity of a chamber
  C_r^ord   = ordered r-tuples without repetition
  C_r^unord = unordered r-subsets

Binary chambers (Third Figure):
  |C_2^unord| = C(n,2) = n(n-1)/2
      n=9  -> 36 chambers
      n=10 -> 45 chambers
  Each chamber may be read in two directions (subject-predicate swap)
      -> 72 directed propositions for n=9
  |C_2^ord| = P(n,2) = n(n-1)
      n=9  -> 72
      n=10 -> 90

Ternary chambers (Fourth Figure / Table):
  |C_3^ord| = P(n,3) = n(n-1)(n-2)
      n=9  -> 504
  Quotient by cyclic permutation of the three letters:
      |C_3^unord| = C(n,3)
      n=9  -> 84 distinct unordered triples
  Great Table inserts marker T in every slot and mixes Fig.A columns
  with Fig.T columns: 20 typed readings of each of 84 triples
      -> 1680 compartments (many semantically redundant)

General r-ary:
  |C_r^ord|   = P(n,r) = n! / (n-r)!
  |C_r^unord| = C(n,r) = n! / (r! (n-r)!)

Leibniz remark: Llull stopped at r=2,3 while the full non-empty
power set of a 9-letter column has 2^9 - 1 = 511 combinations.

3. COMPOSITION OPERATOR AND SEMANTIC MAP
----------------------------------------
Binary composition:
  circ : Lambda x Lambda -> Prop

Realised by sort-sensitive interpretation Phi:
  Phi( (lambda,s), (mu,t) )
    = proposition reading lambda under sort s as subject
      and mu under sort t as predicate

Canonical examples:
  both Dignity:     B circ C  =  "Bonitas est magna"
                                 "Goodness is great"
  Dignity + Rel:    B circ C  =  "Bonitas est differens"
                                 or "Goodness contains difference"
  Q + Dig + Rel:    typed triple BCTB
                    = "Utrum Bonitas sit Differentia?"

circ is neither associative nor commutative in general.
Subject-predicate polarity and chosen sorts matter.

Convertibility inside God (A-centre):
  every dignity may be predicated of every other dignity
  salva veritate.

4. ROTATIONAL GROUP AND EQUIVARIANCE
------------------------------------
Wheels realise cyclic group:
  C_n = < rho | rho^n = 1 >

Action on letters:
  rho(lambda_i) = lambda_{i+1 mod n}

Componentwise on tuples:
  rho . (lambda_i1, ..., lambda_ir)
    = (rho(lambda_i1), ..., rho(lambda_ir))

Semantic equivariance (same-column readings):
  Phi(rho lambda, rho mu) = rho_* Phi(lambda, mu)
  where rho_* permutes the generated propositions.

Different-column readings: rotation still generates new questions,
but content is a new typed combination, not a mere relabeling.

Three-wheel volvelle configuration space:
  (C_n x C_n x C_n) / C_n
  (simultaneous rotation of all three rings is a global symmetry
   that does not change relative alignment)

5. OPERATOR ALGEBRA
-------------------
Heterogeneous algebra:
  L = < Lambda,  { circ_{s,t} }_{s,t in S},  rho,  Phi >

Each circ_{s,t} is sort-restricted composition.
Closed under rotation in the equivariant sense above.

Correlative operators (internal dynamics of a dignity):
  alpha(Dignity) = agent
  pi(Dignity)    = patient
  epsilon(Dignity) = act

Every dignity expands to the triad { alpha, pi, epsilon }.

6. RDG-COMPATIBLE MAPPING (SID-PED)
-----------------------------------
SID triad: Structure-Interaction-Dynamics
PED triad: Power-Evaluation-Dynamics

Treat each typed atom as an RDG object and each composition as an edge.

Homomorphism of operator systems:
  h : L -> RDG
sends each letter to an SID-PED triad and each circ to the
corresponding interaction or evaluation edge.
Rotation rho becomes an RDG automorphism preserving structural
skeleton and dynamical flow.
